## Context

Found during the 2026-07-29 housekeeping sweep: a fresh worktree render of
`deliverables/data-paper/data-paper.qmd` fails on
`{{< include ../_shared/tables/tab_corpus_sources.md >}}` — the `.md`
renderings of the shared tables are gitignored while their `.csv` twins are
tracked. `rules/git.md` says handoff artifacts a downstream workpackage
consumes are durable state and stay committed; a Phase-3 clean-room render
must work from tracked artifacts alone (`manuscript.mk` doctrine). Today it
does not: it needs a prior Phase-2 run or a copy from another checkout.

## Actions

1. Decide the shape: track the generated `.md` tables (align with the
   handoff-artifact rule), or make the render targets depend on the Phase-2
   rules that produce them (weakens the clean-room split).
2. Apply to every gitignored file in the data paper's include closure
   (sweep all deliverables, not just data-paper — `paths.mk` lists them).
3. Extend `tests/test_deliverable_artifacts.py` (or a sibling) so an
   include pointing at an untracked file fails.

## Verification

- [ ] `quarto render deliverables/data-paper/data-paper.qmd` succeeds in a
      fresh worktree with no Phase-2 run and no manual copying.

## Invariants

- No Phase-3 rule triggers Phase 2 (architecture.md: never let a later
  phase trigger an earlier one).

## Exit criteria

- [ ] Clean-room render of every submission deliverable passes from a fresh
      worktree
- [ ] Guard added so the next untracked include fails a test, not a render